  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting participation and the defence of environmental rights of indigenous communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Network for Citizen Participation and Social Control (Red PCCS) in Bolivia is an association civil society institutions that work together to promote participation in the design of public policies and social control of public administration through a rights-based approach. This new project with PCCS seeks to contribute to the defence of environmental, indigenous and human rights based in the framework of Care for our Common Home in four regions across Bolivia. 

The team will work support new young women and men leaders from indigenous campesino communities, with teams of environmental volunteers operating in these regions and with civil society organisations from the PCCS network to strengthen capacities to defend environmental and indigenous rights and develop greater coordination and collaboration between the diverse project participants.</narrative>
  </description>
